  - The documentation (docs/, wiki/) and figures that contain no
    identifiable patient information are licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0.
  - The thesis or technical memoir, when available in memoria/, is
    licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0.
  - Third-party material — pre-trained voice cloning models (e.g.,
    XTTS-v2 under the Coqui Public Model License), anti-spoofing
    detectors (e.g., AASIST under its own research license),
    speech-to-text models (e.g., Whisper under MIT License) and any
    referenced audio datasets — retains its original license. This
    work only references, evaluates and integrates such material; it
    does not redistribute model weights or datasets.

